{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788542373878508001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"mucky-statuesque-akitainu","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b8d2d77b382c16c16d87647882c0be23e994d3199ac37ecc32d6ad757c736c42","event_uuid":"d2af8dcd-846e-4d16-b0e0-b2ce68467002","position":{"commit_sha":"a4afcd983fa3a10270b276807aedc26e6c1981a2","position":"1788528618546446001-d2af8dcd-846e-4d16-b0e0-b2ce68467002"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d2985a1a9f8f3a7edbff754396d4e2f01808aae76d11f842dc3dfd41b4ba526e","event_uuid":"84268d8d-e9a6-4a7a-961b-b6d1b5764623","position":{"commit_sha":"f1cd29deb420077d24d51c5412be47024053adfc","position":"1788528642257801001-84268d8d-e9a6-4a7a-961b-b6d1b5764623"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788528618546446001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Symptom\n\nAn agent following AGENTS.md's orphan-prevention guidance **still leaked a process**: an orphaned\n`zsh` reparented to PID 1, burning **87% CPU**, from a bounded contention run. It was caught only\nbecause the agent independently ran `scripts/check_orphaned_load.py`; nothing in the prescribed\npattern reaped it.\n\nThis matters more than a single stray process. That AGENTS.md section exists specifically to prevent\na documented incident in which **38 processes orphaned to PID 1 and ran for four days** at ~1341%\ncombined CPU, pushing load average to 58 and silently poisoning every timing-sensitive measurement\ntaken in that window. Guidance that does not actually prevent the thing it was written for is worse\nthan none, because it produces confident compliance.\n\n## Two independent gaps, both observed on 2026-09-04\n\n**1. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host.** AGENTS.md's primary bound is:\n\n```sh\ntimeout 120 python -c 'while True: pass' &\n```\n\nThere is no `timeout` and no `gtimeout` here (no coreutils). The command returns **127** and the\nthing you meant to bound **never runs at all** — a silent no-op that looks like success. I hit this\nmyself: a command I believed was bounded simply did not execute, and I only noticed because its\noutput was missing. On a host where the primary bound is unavailable, every reader of that section\neither fails silently or improvises.\n\nA working substitute exists: `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV' <cmd>`.\n\n**2. `trap 'kill 0' EXIT INT TERM` inside a subshell did not reap the wrapper.** AGENTS.md presents\nthe trap as the belt-and-braces sweep, saying it \"signals the entire process group, so it reaps\nhelpers you forgot about\". In the observed case the trap was inside a subshell and the surviving\nprocess was the **wrapper**, outside the group the trap signalled. The claim is true only at the\nright scope, and the document does not say what that scope is.\n\n## Why this is worth fixing rather than absorbing\n\nEvery subagent brief in this repository repeats this guidance, so a gap here propagates to every\nagent that spawns anything. Tonight it propagated to at least one, which then leaked exactly the\nclass of process the section exists to prevent — while believing it had complied.\n\nNote also that `scripts/check_orphaned_load.py` **worked**, and is what caught it. The detector is\nsound; the prevention advice is what failed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nDeterministic and verifiable in a single run — no \"watch for orphans over N days\".\n\n1. AGENTS.md's orphan-prevention section gives a bound that **works on this repository's supported\n   developer platforms**, macOS included. If `timeout` is retained as the primary example, the\n   section must state that it is absent on macOS and give the working alternative alongside it — not\n   in a footnote.\n2. The `trap 'kill 0'` guidance states the **scope** it operates at and what it does not cover, or is\n   replaced by a pattern that reaps a wrapper spawned from a subshell. Demonstrate with a real\n   spawn/teardown that a wrapper does not survive.\n3. **Defect-seeded:** run the documented pattern as written today on macOS and show the bound not\n   taking effect (exit 127, command never runs); then show the corrected guidance bounding the same\n   command. Both in one run.\n4. Any check added is portable — no CI provider required — per the blocking `project.portability`\n   criterion. `check_orphaned_load.py` is the model: read-only, on-demand, no CI dependency.\n\n## Not in scope\n\nWiring an orphan check into `make lint`. `check_orphaned_load.py` is deliberately excluded because it\nreports on **live host state**, not on the tree under review, and that reasoning is sound and\ndocumented. This ticket is about the **prevention advice**, not the detector.\n\n## File impact\n\n`AGENTS.md` (the \"Bound every background process you spawn\" section).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"the 'Bound every background process you spawn' section: its primary bound (timeout) does not exist on macOS and returns 127 so the command silently never runs, and its trap 'kill 0' sweep is described as reaping the entire process group without stating the scope at which that holds -- a wrapper spawned from a subshell survived it"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["bug","docs","agents","portability","process-hygiene"],"ticket_id":"0d6c-b19b-0de7-432e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"AGENTS.md orphan-prevention guidance does not work on macOS: timeout is absent (exit 127, silent no-op) and trap 'kill 0' in a subshell left a wrapper at PPID 1","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d2af8dcd-846e-4d16-b0e0-b2ce68467002","84268d8d-e9a6-4a7a-961b-b6d1b5764623"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788542373878508001,"uuid":"1d0359cd-9df2-4cb6-b435-3554b6594c26"}